& [ExistingConstructionPatternAudit] finds a reusable safe boundary
  + current plan and request types are strict Deserialize forms with deny_unknown_fields, private or narrowly exposed fields, exact profiles, and pure validation
  + current assembly, digest, reconciliation scope, disposition, and reconciliation result types are output-only Serialize values
  + derived output fields are private and exposed through read-only getters
  + only current pure derivation functions construct the output-only values in production code
  + module-local tests may construct private fixtures without exposing a production constructor
  + this pattern supports caller-inspectable inputs and non-forgeable-by-serde derived results without introducing capability secrets

& [ConstructionBoundaryDecision] is complete deferral of admitted provenance
  + profile 0.1 defines no AdmittedAcquisitionLineage production wrapper
  + profile 0.1 defines no public, crate-public, trait, token, key, registry, or constructor that can confer physical acquisition authority
  + public strict claim forms may be decoded and validated only as claims
  + structurally derived claim results are output-only Serialize values with private fields and read-only getters
  + later M2C owns the separate physical output wrapper and its narrow construction path after successful authorized observation
  + a future M2C source must bind construction capability, actual control-flow evidence, provenance grade, and test-production separation
  + source revision is unnecessary because the source explicitly allowed complete deferral

& [IdentityRepresentationAudit] selects bounded logical identity for full SJS
  + existing current pure plans use nonzero u64 identities for assembly, commitment, reconciliation, projection, batch, and entry-reference correlation
  + one private-field AcquisitionIdentity wrapper over nonzero u64 is representation-feasible, canonical, bounded, allocation-free, and round-trip stable
  + zero is invalid and exact equality and inequality are deterministic
  + caller choice establishes only logical correlation, not uniqueness, generation, event occurrence, or physical provenance
  + no random source, clock, UUID generator, database sequence, process state, or global collision registry is selected
  + later M2C must define the collision domain and bind producer-admitted uniqueness before an identity becomes physical provenance

& [ComparisonScopeAudit] prevents redundant identity inflation
  + complete AcquisitionScopeClaim already supplies the semantic comparison coordinates
  + a separate opaque comparison-scope identity would add caller correlation without proving scope equality
  + profile 0.1 should compare the complete scope product structurally and derive any stable scope commitment only if full SJS proves a consumer need
  + the speculative comparison-scope identity field is therefore a pruning candidate rather than a mandatory new primitive

& [ScopeReuseAudit] is feasible with current exact forms
  + root strong identity reuses current root volume serial and file-id meaning
  + canonical volume-GUID path and candidate-root representation reuse current topology validation where available
  + TopologyScanLimits is reused as one complete current bounded value
  + scanner, machine forms, topology forms, receipt, assembly, digest, reconciliation, and ordered encoding profiles remain exact closed constants
  + policy digest and predecessor receipt digest remain exact lowercase SHA-256 syntax under current helpers or equivalent bounded validators
  + predecessor admission profile is exact and bounded
  + SJS must decide whether redundant coordinates are stored or derived, but may not omit any comparison coordinate

& [LineageOwnershipAudit] selects complete owned carriers
  + each AcquisitionLineageClaim owns one complete current output-only ordered digest carrier
  + that digest carrier already owns its complete supplied inventory assembly carrier and all transitive ancestry
  + duplicating both assembly and digest as peer fields would permit divergence and enlarge the validation surface
  + validation must still independently rederive the digest from its owned assembly before accepting the lineage claim
  + no bare digest string, loose assembly, caller summary, external reference lookup, database key, or lazy file locator is accepted
  + first and second carriers remain independently owned and cannot alias by role substitution

& [CompletionDispositionAudit] prunes speculative lifecycle
  + successful profile 0.1 evidence input needs only CompleteClaimed
  + IncompleteClaimed and FaultedClaimed do not enable a current consumer and would mix runtime lifecycle into a pure successful claim form
  + full SJS should model completion as an exact closed CompleteClaimed token or an invariant of the accepted lineage type
  + no token may say Observed, Actual, Proven, Trusted, Admitted, Issued, Stable, Quiescent, or Snapshot

& [CausalOrderAudit] remains effect free
  + one closed relation kind FirstCompletionStrictlyPrecedesSecondStart is sufficient for profile 0.1
  + the relation binds the exact first and second AcquisitionIdentity values in explicit roles
  + pure validation checks nonzero identities, inequality, role equality, and supported direction
  + vector order, JSON order, field names, caller ordinals, digest operands, or increasing numbers never substitute for the causal relation
  + no clock field, tick domain, duration, freshness, wall time, monotonic time, or time API is required or authorized
  + later M2C must prove the relation from actual control flow or separately governed observation

& [ReconciliationAndEvidenceAudit] prevents semantic laundering
  + one strict repeated-inventory plan binds the complete ordered pair and exact current reconciliation plan
  + current reconciliation independently rederives both digest carriers and returns only Equal or Different
  + Different is a successful comparison disposition but a typed failure for requested repeated-equality evidence
  + Equal is necessary but remains insufficient without distinct acquisitions, exact order, common scope, and production provenance
  + successful pure derivation yields a ClaimOnly evidence record naming NonAtomicRepeatedInventoryEqual
  + OsSnapshotProven is structurally rejected because no snapshot primitive or provenance exists
  + no direct From, Into, constructor, or method converts the claim result to TopologyReceipt or issued evidence

& [SerdeAndVisibilityAudit] is strict
  + caller-authored claim inputs may derive Serialize and Deserialize with deny_unknown_fields
  + closed enums use exact named variants and no catch-all
  + output-only claim results derive Serialize but not Deserialize or Default
  + output-only fields are private and visible through read-only getters
  + no aliases, defaults, flattening, untagged enums, maps, arbitrary JSON, free-form diagnostic payloads, or compatibility fallback exists
  + one public pure derivation function may construct the output-only claim result after complete validation
  + module visibility remains the narrowest compatible with future separately governed M2C integration

& [SyntheticTestBoundaryAudit] is explicit
  + synthetic carrier construction remains inside module-local cfg(test) code or existing pure derivation helpers
  + no test-only constructor is compiled into a production build
  + fixture values are claims and never use admitted, actual, observed, issuer, or trusted vocabulary
  + static tests must prove output-only results lack Deserialize, unrestricted constructor, and direct receipt conversion surfaces
  + future physical fixtures remain separately sourced, disposable, supervised, and unauthorized by this slice

& [FaultAndResourceAudit] is bounded
  + one closed fault code taxonomy may cover InvalidRequest, Profile, Identity, Scope, Lineage, Order, Reconciliation, Different, Evidence, and Resource
  + Capability is unnecessary in profile 0.1 because no admitted-construction operation exists to call
  + faults retain bounded field and message text and release no partial output
  + two lineage carriers are exact cardinality; no vector, map, recursion, or arbitrary extension collection is needed
  + nested current bounds are reused and all arithmetic remains checked
  + validation and rederivation remain bounded by the two current carrier sizes

& [ThreatAudit] passes for full SJS routing
  + deserialize-laundering is blocked by claim-only semantics and output-only derived results
  + constructor-laundering is blocked because no admitted wrapper or production capability exists
  + fixture-laundering is blocked by cfg(test) isolation and explicit synthetic claim vocabulary
  + equality-laundering is blocked because Equal remains one subordinate relation
  + order-laundering is blocked by explicit identities and a closed causal role edge
  + scope-laundering is blocked by exact complete structural equality
  + lineage-laundering is blocked by owning the complete digest carrier and independently rederiving it
  + receipt-laundering is blocked by absence of conversion and issuer surfaces
  + opacity loss is avoided because every claim and output retains inspectable serialized lineage

& [ImplementationFeasibilityAudit] is pure and bounded
  + at most one new safe-Rust module plus one lib export is sufficient after exact signed authority
  + existing serde, serde_json, error, SHA-256 validation, topology, carrier, and reconciliation facilities are sufficient
  + no Cargo.toml or Cargo.lock change is needed
  + no unsafe or platform-specific cfg is needed
  + no Windows, filesystem, handle, pointer, clock, random, process, environment, network, persistence, database, Git runtime, model, tool, or effect import is needed
  + production and Cargo trees remain byte unchanged during this audit

& [RequirementAudit] accepts P3TALF-001 through P3TALF-014
  + exact source, predecessor, profile, and module binding
  + claim versus producer-admitted provenance separation
  + bounded logical acquisition identity without uniqueness inflation
  + complete exact scope product without wildcard
  + complete independent lineage ownership and rederivation
  + distinct ordered roles and claimed causal relation without clocks
  + current reconciliation and Equal requirement
  + ClaimOnly repeated-inventory evidence with no receipt conversion
  + complete deferral of production-admitted wrapper to M2C
  + strict serde, visibility, deterministic validation, and resources
  + closed atomic fault taxonomy
  + adversarial provenance-laundering and construction tests
  + one-module, zero-dependency, zero-effect candidate boundary
  + full SJS, phase lock, proof, evidence, provenance, rollback, nonclaims, and publication closure

& [ConflictAudit] finds no source correction
  + source alternatives are resolved within their expressly delegated SJS decisions
  + complete deferral is one source-authorized construction-boundary option
  + nonzero u64 wrapper is one source-authorized existing bounded identity reuse
  + structural scope equality is consistent with the source and makes a speculative comparison identity unnecessary
  + owning the current digest carrier preserves the required assembly ancestry without peer duplication
  + pruning unused completion variants and Capability fault narrows rather than changes intent
  + no existing type or profile mismatch prevents full SJS

& [EffectAudit] passes
  + production and Cargo trees remain byte unchanged
  + no scanner, acquisition, platform call, filesystem access, clock read, randomness, fixture execution, producer admission, evidence issuance, receipt issuance, consumption, mutation, seal, cleanup, promotion, neural routing, distributed inference, FPGA execution, or other effect is selected
  + references to later M2C behavior are requirements and nonclaims, never transitive authority

